"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:c3ce65839a10a5966721d3b8"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D. 2.37","reason":"The triangle has legs 1 and √3 and hypotenuse 2. For the large circle, the tangent lengths from B and C give (r-1)+(r-√3)=2. Hence r=(3+√3)/2≈2.36603, which rounds to 2.37.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h170"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1997_AMC_12_Q19","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"center-to-line-distance","label":"Center-to-line distance","methodDirectNodeIds":{"center-to-line-distance":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:c3ce65839a10a5966721d3b8"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: 3(10 - √2)/28","reason":"The angle-bisector theorem gives AD = 15/7 and BD = 20/7. The equal distances from D to the two legs are 12/7, so CD = 12√2/7. Using r = area/semiperimeter gives r_a = 3/(3 + √2) and r_b = 4/(4 + √2). Their ratio simplifies to 3(10 - √2)/28.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h170"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2008_AMC_12A_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"incenter-coordinate-distances","label":"Use equidistant incenter coordinates","methodDirectNodeIds":{"incenter-coordinate-distances":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:c3ce65839a10a5966721d3b8"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A, (32√3-24)/13","reason":"Take C=(0,0), A=(4,0), B=(0,3), so the hypotenuse is 3u+4v=12. A ray at angle θ has length L=12/(3cosθ+4sinθ). The shorter length is at θ=60°: L=24/(3+4√3)=(32√3-24)/13.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h170"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1960_AMC_12_Q40","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"intersect-trisector-rays","label":"Intersect coordinate rays","methodDirectNodeIds":{"intersect-trisector-rays":["cnm_h170","cnm_276","cnm_277"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h170","cnm_276","cnm_277"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:c3ce65839a10a5966721d3b8"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 2","reason":"For intercepts p and b, 4/p+3/b=1 gives b=3+12/(p-4), with p>4. Thus p-4 divides 12. Only p=5 and p=7 are prime possibilities, giving b=15 and b=7.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h170"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1994_AMC_12_Q28","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p153","cnm_p157"],"id":"positive-divisor-search","label":"Reduce the intercept restrictions to divisors","methodDirectNodeIds":{"positive-divisor-search":["cnm_h170","math:integer-diophantine-equations"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h170","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_p153","cnm_p157"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:c3ce65839a10a5966721d3b8"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D. 145/147","reason":"The hypotenuse is 5 and the field area is 6. If the square's side is s, joining its opposite corner to the field's vertices gives 6=(5·2)/2+(3s)/2+(4s)/2. Hence s=2/7, and the planted fraction is 1−(2/7)²/6=145/147.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h170"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2018_AMC_12A_Q17","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"coordinate-line-distance","label":"Coordinate point-to-line distance","methodDirectNodeIds":{"coordinate-line-distance":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:c3ce65839a10a5966721d3b8"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E (17)","reason":"Tangency gives r=(a+b-c)/2 or r=(a+b+c)/2. The first case corresponds to positive ordered factors uv=2r², with a=2r+u and b=2r+v. The second corresponds to factors satisfying r<u,v<2r. The total segment counts for r=1,...,6 are 2,4,6,6,6,14. At r=6, the smallest and largest hypotenuses are 5 from (3,4,5) and 85 from (13,84,85). Thus c14/c1=85/5=17.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h170"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2022_AMC_12A_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"distance-to-intercept-line","label":"Apply the line-circle distance condition","methodDirectNodeIds":{"distance-to-intercept-line":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174","cnm_h179","cnm_174","math:integer-diophantine-equations","math:divisor-count-and-sum"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h170","cnm_h174","cnm_h179","cnm_174","math:integer-diophantine-equations","math:divisor-count-and-sum"]}]}],"canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h170"],"label":"直线的截距式","layer":"CN","meaning":"Practice covers aligned canonical concepts, with no claim of complete standard coverage or mastery.","nextOffset":null,"sourceNode":{"criteria":["能从截距式读出横截距和纵截距","知道过原点的直线不能写成截距式"],"description":"与两条坐标轴分别交于 (a，0)、(0，b) 且 a、b 都不为 0 的直线，可以写成 x/a+y/b=1。","id":"cnm_h170","label":"直线的截距式","original":{"chapter":"选必一 第二章 直线和圆的方程 2.2","description":"与两条坐标轴分别交于 (a，0)、(0，b) 且 a、b 都不为 0 的直线，可以写成 x/a+y/b=1。","domain":"图形与几何","external":false,"grade":12,"id":"cnm_h170","mastery_criteria":["能从截距式读出横截距和纵截距","知道过原点的直线不能写成截距式"],"name":"直线的截距式","semester":"上","standards":[{"confidence":"inferred","id":"cms-2017:H.GA.17","note":"截距式是两点式的一种写法。待核。"}],"type":"procedural"},"placement":{"bookCode":"12","bookLabel":"选必一","chapter":"选必一 第二章 直线和圆的方程 2.2","domain":"图形与几何","semester":"上"},"reviewStatus":"source_only"},"sourceNodeId":"cnm_h170","status":"mapped","total":11}
